# Live test 4: OSM notes. Creates a note in open ocean near lat -48, lon -123 on
# the development server, comments on it, closes it, reopens it and closes it
# again, so the note ends up closed. Notes cannot be deleted; a closed test note
# is the cleanest state possible.
#
#   cargo run -- --api-server dev --script-delay-ms 400 --script docs/live-test/04-notes.osmscript
#
# Sign in first with 00-sign-in.osmscript. If you signed in before the Notes
# feature existed, sign in again: the saved login lacks the write_notes scope
# and the server answers 403 (the note panel then says to sign in again).
# Captures go to out/live-04-*.png. Window 1200x800.
#
# Every note write here refuses to run unless the active server is the OSM
# development server.

assert_server dev
assert_signed_in
window 1200 800
viewport -48.0 -123.0 12
wait_idle 10s
show_notes on
assert_dialog none

pause 1s Creating a test note
new_note -48.0 -123.0 osm-gpui live test: please ignore this note
# new_note turns Notes on and opens the new note in the side panel.
assert_note_status open
assert_note_comments 1
capture out/live-04-01-created.png

pause 1s Commenting
note_comment second comment from the osm-gpui live test
assert_note_comments 2
capture out/live-04-02-commented.png

pause 1s Closing
note_close closing the osm-gpui live test note
assert_note_status closed
assert_note_comments 3
capture out/live-04-03-closed.png

pause 1s Reopening
note_reopen reopening for the live test
assert_note_status open
assert_note_comments 4
capture out/live-04-04-reopened.png

pause 1s Closing again
note_close done, the osm-gpui live test is finished
assert_note_status closed
assert_note_comments 5
capture out/live-04-05-closed-again.png
pause 2s Notes live test finished: the test note is closed
log done
